/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The method may be used when there are at least three continuous spans each way, panels are rectangular with long/short span ≤ 2, successive spans differ by no more than one-third of the longer, columns are offset by at most 10 % of the span
   - W = wu l₂ lₙ is the total design load on the panel width l₂ over the clear span lₙ (kN). lₙ runs between the faces of the columns or capitals, but is not taken less than 0.65l₁.
   - End spans use other fractions that depend on how stiff the outer column is, and the column strip takes all of the negative moment at an exterior support.
   - A column can punch through the slab along a truncated cone or pyramid.
*/
