/* book: lead: Yield line theory finds the load at which a reinforced concrete slab collapses. At collapse the under-reinforced slab cracks and yields along straight lines, the yield lines, which cut it into flat pieces that rotate like a mechanism. Equating the work done by the load to the work absorbed in the yield lines gives the collapse load. It suits slabs of any shape and support, where tables do not exis */
