/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Along a yield line the steel has yielded and the slab rotates at a constant moment m per metre of line, the moment of resistance of the section (kN·m/m).
   - Give the mechanism a small deflection δ at its deepest point.
   - Every possible mechanism gives a load at or above the true collapse load: the method is an upper bound.
*/
